From a5b850afb3314d17c331ef4544f9c77984c3bb44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Liam Fucich <liam.fucich@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 22:04:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Xkntt: instruction semantics and the Tier-2 coprocessor
 model

Adds the extension's implementation as new files only.  Nothing includes them
yet, so this commit is behaviourally identical to its parent; the wiring is the
next commit.  The split is deliberate: upstream churn lands on the integration
patch, never on this one, which keeps rebasing onto a new Spike cheap.

riscv/xkntt_encoding.h holds MATCH/MASK/DECLARE_INSN for all ten instructions.
The masks encode two rules that are easy to miss.  Within custom-0, funct3 in
{3,4} selects the R4 format, so kbmul0 and kmac leave bits 31:27 free for rs3
and constrain only funct2.  And reserved register fields are strict -- folded
into the mask, so a nonzero value decodes to nothing and traps.  That is
docs/isa-spec.md Deviation 3, and it matters because plan A3 compares the RTL
decoder against a Python decoder over a million random words; a lax Spike and a
strict RTL would disagree on exactly those words.

riscv/xkntt.h carries the Montgomery and Barrett primitives and the coefficient
packing helpers, transcribed from the reference with its lazy (unreduced)
output ranges intact.  The truncations are load-bearing: normalising would
break bit-exactness against the C reference, which everything else rests on.

riscv/insns/*.h are the ten instruction bodies.  Note kbfgs multiplies by
(b - a), matching fqmul(zeta, r[j+len] - r[j]) in the reference -- the plan's
proposed text says (a - b), which is the negation and would make INTT wrong.

riscv/xkntt.cc models the Tier-2 coprocessor: an abstract_device_t holding two
512-byte polynomial buffers, plus forward NTT, inverse NTT and basemul.  The
zeta table is generated from the root of unity rather than hard-coded, per plan
B0.  The aperture layout, the kntt.cfg descriptor and the basemul operand
convention are PROVISIONAL and marked as such -- docs/isa-spec.md section 9
defers them to Track B.  CYCLES is a model (P=4 lanes), not a measurement:
Spike is functional, so BUSY is never observably set and the adversarial cases
in plan I2 can only be exercised in RTL.
